{
  "source": "course-assets/does-ai-think/does-ai-think.mp4",
  "duration": 200.3413125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.96,
      "text": "You type a question into an interface, and the machine types back like a person."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.54,
      "end": 10.46,
      "text": "It explains complex topics, tells jokes, and even says sorry when it slips up."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.14,
      "end": 14.74,
      "text": "After a few minutes, it's hard not to feel like someone is in there."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.26,
      "end": 16.52,
      "text": "So here is the big question."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.14,
      "end": 19.08,
      "text": "Does AI actually think?"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.88,
      "end": 23.7,
      "text": "When it gives you a human-like answer, is it understanding things the way you do?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.32,
      "end": 27.44,
      "text": "There is no denying that conversational capabilities are impressive."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.44,
      "end": 32.52,
      "text": "These systems can finish your sentence, write working code, and explain a poem."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.28,
      "end": 37.84,
      "text": "But sounding like a person doesn't tell you whether it understands things the way a person does."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.62,
      "end": 42.96,
      "text": "There is a famous way to picture this problem. It is a thought experiment known as the Chinese room."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.72,
      "end": 47.42,
      "text": "Imagine a person locked in a room who does not know a single word of Chinese."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.0,
      "end": 51.24,
      "text": "This diagram shows exactly how the Chinese room works step by step."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.86,
      "end": 55.9,
      "text": "In step one, people on the outside slide a note written in Chinese under the door."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.9,
      "end": 57.72,
      "text": "the text asks, how are you?"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.32,
      "end": 61.08,
      "text": "In step two, the person inside looks at the paper."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.62,
      "end": 64.52,
      "text": "They can't read it, so they look up the entire phrase"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.52,
      "end": 66.04,
      "text": "on a giant chart on the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.08,
      "end": 68.84,
      "text": "In step three, they follow the rule book"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.84,
      "end": 70.56,
      "text": "to find the required response,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.16,
      "end": 73.66,
      "text": "write out the matching reply, meaning I'm fine,"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.82,
      "end": 76.5,
      "text": "thank you, and slide it back to the people outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.42,
      "end": 78.36,
      "text": "To anyone outside,"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.56,
      "end": 80.48,
      "text": "it looks like fluent Chinese conversation."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.3,
      "end": 83.78,
      "text": "A convincing answer doesn't prove understanding."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.78,
      "end": 90.9,
      "text": "The Chinese room illustrates a distinction. Producing an answer and understanding it aren't necessarily the same thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.98,
      "end": 98.14,
      "text": "An LLM doesn't follow a literal rulebook. It uses patterns learned during training to predict its response."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.74,
      "end": 102.06,
      "text": "When searchers asked Google how to keep cheese from sliding off a pizza,"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.66,
      "end": 107.94,
      "text": "the AI confidently suggested mixing about 1 eighth of a cup of non-toxic glue into the sauce."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.66,
      "end": 111.62,
      "text": "That bizarre advice traced back to an old joke on a Reddit thread."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.62,
      "end": 115.6,
      "text": "The user wrote the joke in a deadpan tone of sincere cooking advice."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.42,
      "end": 118.44,
      "text": "This diagram shows exactly what went wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.08,
      "end": 123.68,
      "text": "The AI successfully found real text, but completely missed the human context and meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.26,
      "end": 126.84,
      "text": "The Reddit comment was real. The cooking advice was not."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.54,
      "end": 130.84,
      "text": "The source existed, but the AI interpreted it incorrectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.9,
      "end": 136.1,
      "text": "This table directly compares what happens when you think with what an AI does."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.84,
      "end": 138.64,
      "text": "First, look at experience and meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.64,
      "end": 144.92,
      "text": "You draw on things you have actually lived through, connecting words to physical and emotional realities in your life."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.78,
      "end": 150.02,
      "text": "AI strictly uses learned data patterns and whatever information you tell it in the prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.86,
      "end": 155.28,
      "text": "For word choice, you actively select words to express what you want to say."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.96,
      "end": 159.34,
      "text": "AI algorithmically predicts the next word, then repeats."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.32,
      "end": 162.08,
      "text": "Finally, look at uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.74,
      "end": 165.04,
      "text": "You can notice when you are unsure."
    },
    {
      "start": 165.04,
      "end": 171.16,
      "text": "AI can sound certain even when it is wrong. Similar looking answers can come"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.16,
      "end": 175.82,
      "text": "from very different processes. Pointing this out does not mean artificial"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.82,
      "end": 180.42,
      "text": "intelligence is useless. These tools can summarize legal documents, write complex"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.42,
      "end": 184.38,
      "text": "code, and do highly impressive valuable work at massive scale."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.02,
      "end": 188.88,
      "text": "Generating an output that sounds like a person is never enough evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 188.88,
      "end": 193.54,
      "text": "to show that the machine understands the world the way you do. Sounds human,"
    },
    {
      "start": 193.54,
      "end": 195.14,
      "text": "works differently."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.88,
      "end": 198.58,
      "text": "A convincing answer doesn't prove understanding."
    }
  ],
